<title>USA: ServiceMaster completes Barefoot review.</title>
<headline>ServiceMaster completes Barefoot review.</headline>
<dateline>DOWNERS GROVE, Ill. 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>ServiceMaster LP said Thursday it has completed due diligence related to its planned $230 million acquisition of lawncare competitor Barefoot Inc and will proceed with the acquisition.</p>
<p>The transaction is to be carried out through a tender offer in which ServiceMaster will offer Barefoot stockholders their choice of $16 a share in either cash or an equivalent amount of ServiceMaster shares, the company said.</p>
<p>The transaction still requires U.S. anti-trust clearance and approval by holders of at least 75 percent of Barefoot's 14.5 million shares, the company said.</p>
<p>Barefoot shares rose 1/16 to 15-1/2 Thursday, while ServiceMaster rose 1/4 to 25-3/4.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
